/.lake

# LaTeX build artifacts
*.aux
*.fdb_latexmk
*.fls
*.log
*.out
*.synctex.gz

# PDFs (papers and build output)
*.pdf

# Writing about the project, as opposed to the project. Untracked 2026-09-06 before the
# first push; both stay on disk.
/Cheval.tex

# The reference document's LaTeX sources. Not our development, and its PDF was already
# excluded by the *.pdf rule above, which left the repo tracking sources for a build it
# could not run. Untracked 2026-09-06 before the first push; the directory stays on disk.
/Metateorema-New3/

# LaTeX build artifacts of docs/report/. The sources ARE tracked; report.pdf is not, because
# of the *.pdf rule above — build it with `make` in docs/report/.
docs/report/*.out
docs/report/*.toc

# NOTE: hilbert-out/ and term-print-out/ ARE tracked, deliberately. They are generated
# (by `#hilbert … to "…"` in Probes/HilbertDemo.lean, and by Probes/TermPrintDemo.lean),
# so they will show up as diffs after a probe run — but they are the project's readable
# output, they cost a full build to regenerate, and they are wanted in a backup.

# Editor / tooling scratch
_mcp_snippet_*.lean
*.bak
.claude/memory/
.claude/worktrees/
# Local permission/hook config. Also covered by a global ignore on this machine, but that
# does not travel with the repo — keep it here so a fresh clone is safe too.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Agent worktrees (git worktree add .worktrees/<name>); branches live in .git regardless
/.worktrees/

/AML-Formalization
